// What a unit is worth in a fight, in High Men spearmen (a recruit High Men spearman is 1): the
// fit of `f4x-tools duel ladder` over real battles (task 655, `docs/duel.md`). `levels` is the worth at
// experience level 1, 2, ... as far as it was measured (6 for a normal unit, 9 for a hero, one number for a
// creature, which does not level); a higher level takes the last number. It is a rough guide, a
// few percent either way: two units of 100 are worth one of 200, and rock-paper-scissors cases
// (immunities, special attacks) can overturn it. A hero was fought with the abilities and spells the
// game rolls for a hero (no items), so `hero_factor` is 1.
// Written by `f4x-tools duel ladder --combine 1-9 --ratings FILE`; no unit of the settler kind.
(
    hero_factor: 1.0,
    // What one spearman is in the numbers the AI's thresholds were tuned to: the median of the old formula
    // (`battle::power`) over the worth at level 1 of the units that are not heroes.
